The licensor grants you a copyright license to use the software, and to make the copies of it that using it needs, for a permitted purpose only. The licensor reserves every right these terms do not grant.

## Permitted Purposes

These are the only permitted purposes:

- **Educational use.** Learning or teaching: a student's study or coursework, or a teacher's or instructor's teaching of a course, including demonstrating the software to a class. Testing or maintaining any website or system that an educational institution runs is not educational use.

- **Personal projects.** An individual's own website, application or other project, made and kept for themselves, with no commercial use: to generate and run tests that validate it.

Any other use is not a permitted purpose. That includes, whether or not anyone is paid and whether or not it makes a profit, any use:

- by or for a business, a nonprofit or charitable organization, a cooperative, an association, or a government, government agency, military, police, intelligence or security service, or anyone acting for any of them;
- in the course of employment, contracting, consulting, freelancing or any other paid work;
- for a website, application or project that sells, advertises, raises money, or is run for or by any organization;
- to provide a product or service to anyone else, including generating test suites for others.

Such use requires a separate written license from the licensor (see COMMERCIAL-LICENSE.md), which the licensor may grant or decline at the licensor's sole discretion.

## Changes

You may change the software for your own use for a permitted purpose. You may not distribute the software, or any changed version or part of it, to anyone.

## Generated Output

Projects the software generates (its output) are licensed separately, by GENERATED-OUTPUT.md and the LICENSE file each one carries. However it was generated, a project belongs to the owner of what it tests, who needs no license for the software to use it. These terms govern only generating it: generating a project for a purpose these terms do not permit breaks them, but does not take the project from that owner. A project you generate for educational use, of something you do not own, you may use only for that use.

